<title>USA: Electronics Communications warrant change.</title>
<headline>Electronics Communications warrant change.</headline>
<dateline>FAIRFIELD, N.J. 1996-12-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Electronics Communications Corp  said its board authorized a reduction in the conversion price of the company's Class A common stock purchase warrants from $5 to $2.25.</p>
<p>The board also authorized changing the terms of the warrant so the company could call the warrant if it traded at $3.60 or more, for 20 consecutive days, it said.</p>
<p>William Taylor, president and chief executive officer, said: &quot;This reduction in the conversion price of the warrant is intended to encourage further capitalization of the company and to concomitantly enhance shareholder value.&quot;</p>
</text>
